# Component CSS Patterns

## Boilerplate

Every component stylesheet starts with the universal box-sizing reset:

```css
*,
*:after,
*:before {
  box-sizing: border-box;
}

:host {
  display: block;
}
```

## Logical Properties

Always use logical properties instead of physical ones:

- `inline-size` / `block-size` (not `width` / `height`)
- `inset-inline-start` / `inset-block-start` (not `left` / `top`)
- `margin-inline` / `padding-block` (not `margin-left` / `padding-top`)
- `border-inline-start` (not `border-left`)

## Design Tokens

- Public tokens: `--flotsam-<category>-<name>` with hardcoded fallback
- Private/internal tokens: `--_<descriptive-name>` (no namespace, scoped to shadow DOM)
- Always provide a fallback value: `var(--flotsam-space-lg, 16px)`

```css
:host {
  padding: var(--flotsam-space-lg, 16px);
  color: var(--flotsam-color-text-primary);
}

#container {
  gap: var(--_container-gap, var(--flotsam-space-md, 8px));
}
```

## Color Scheme / Dark Mode

Use `light-dark()` for automatic light/dark adaptation:

```css
background-color: light-dark(
  var(--flotsam-color-surface-lightest, #ffffff),
  var(--flotsam-color-surface-darkest, #151515)
);
```

## Responsive Design

Prefer `@container` queries over `@media` queries. Name containers on the host:

```css
:host {
  container: card / inline-size;
}

@container card (min-width: 576px) {
  #content { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
}
```

## Accessibility

Use the `.visually-hidden` pattern for screen-reader-only text:

```css
.visually-hidden {
  position: absolute !important;
  block-size: 1px;
  inline-size: 1px;
  overflow: hidden;
  clip: rect(1px, 1px, 1px, 1px);
  clip-path: inset(50%);
  white-space: nowrap;
  border: 0;
  padding: 0 !important;
  margin: -1px !important;
}
```

## Slotted & Parts

- Style slotted content with `::slotted(<selector>)`
- Expose stylable internals with `part="name"` in the template
- Use CSS nesting freely; it is supported in all target environments
